# exec_zero_length_range_unaligned_isolate: A zero-length range. In-process a range that is not page-aligned makes an empty cursor (LocalTask::cursor walks one page), and an empty cursor has no header: skipped, and the exec completes. A page-aligned one dies in the host. The service refuses every zero length ("Zero length cursor request") and dereferences the null cursor, a death in the task's own code that ends only the task: the exec faults, and so does the next (docs/testing.md, section 6.12).
